sxml xquery - Evaluate an XQuery 4.0 query

Usage: sxml xquery [--context-item=FILE] [--expression=TEXT] [--param=NAME=VALUE]... [--method=METHOD] [QUERY-FILE]

Compiles the XQuery 4.0 main module in QUERY-FILE, or given with
--expression, and writes its result to standard output, serialized as
the query's output declarations say (method xml unless they name
another); --method replaces the method. --context-item=FILE parses
FILE as the context item. --param=NAME=VALUE binds the external
variable $NAME, which the query declares, to xs:untypedAtomic(VALUE).
fn:doc reads local files only. An error of the query is reported on
standard error as QUERY-FILE:LINE:COLUMN: err:CODE: description and
exits 1; an unreadable file exits 3.

Options:
  -h, --help               Show this help and exit
      --context-item=FILE  XML document to use as the context item; - reads standard input
      --expression=TEXT    The query itself, instead of QUERY-FILE
      --param=NAME=VALUE   Bind external variable $NAME to xs:untypedAtomic(VALUE) (repeatable)
      --method=METHOD      Serialization method of the result, replacing the query's (one of: adaptive, xml, xhtml, html, text, json)

Arguments:
  QUERY-FILE  File holding the XQuery 4.0 main module; - reads standard input

Examples:
  sxml xquery report.xq
  sxml xquery --expression='for $i in 1 to 3 return <i>{$i}</i>'
  sxml xquery --context-item=book.xml --method=text titles.xq
  sxml xquery --param=n=5 --expression='declare variable $n external; $n * 2'
